{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785002781,"nonce":"APoSd2Sq45pxXm96YP0mRcySa60=","message":"Fix in PR #81 (branch `fix/dogfood-infra-and-runbook`, commit 90375ef). The SERVER side already ships in full — `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM[_FILE]`, inline-wins precedence, loud boot failure on a bad path, DB `_forge` override, and the startup audit correctly skipping the credential check when a boot PEM is present. Nothing of that was re-implemented. The real gap was DELIVERY: the chart offered the PEM only as an env var and deploy.sh never used it, so the dogfood loop still seeded it via reseed.sh's POST /v1/secrets. Adds `secrets.githubAppPemSecret` projecting an out-of-band Secret read-only at /etc/scarab/forge/, and reseed.sh now detects the mount and skips its PUT. Default helm render unchanged. Leaving open until the PR merges.","files":null}]}